1
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:24,947
A funny story about a family... And the little girl who started it.

2
00:10:37,894 --> 00:10:43,894
Curly Sue is a comedy, drama, family film directed by John Hughes.

3
00:15:56,842 --> 00:16:02,842
Bill is a penniless drifter who scams strangers out of just enough money to feed
himself and his partner in crime, an orphan girl known as Curly Sue.

4
00:21:15,789 --> 00:21:21,789
Bill and Curly Sue target Grey, a yuppie lawyer, but their con takes an unexpected
turn when the successful woman begins to like the ramshackle duo.

5
00:26:34,736 --> 00:26:40,736
But there's one problem—Grey's jealous, conniving boyfriend, Walker.

6
00:31:53,684 --> 00:31:59,684
Bill Dancer, played by Jim Belushi.

7
00:37:12,631 --> 00:37:18,631
Curly Sue, played by Alisan Porter.

8
00:42:31,578 --> 00:42:37,578
Grey Ellison, played by Kelly Lynch.

9
00:47:50,526 --> 00:47:56,526
Walker McCormick, played by John Getz.

10
00:53:09,473 --> 00:53:15,473
Tesio, played by Steve Carell.

11
00:58:28,421 --> 00:58:34,421
Bernard Oxbar, played by Fred Thompson.

12
01:03:47,368 --> 01:03:53,368
Curly Sue is a 1991 American comedy drama film written, produced, and directed by John Hughes, and
starring James Belushi, Kelly Lynch and Alisan Porter with Steve Carell in his film debut.

13
01:09:06,315 --> 01:09:12,315
It tells the story of a homeless con artist and his young orphan
companion who gain shelter with a rich divorce lawyer.

14
01:14:25,263 --> 01:14:31,263
This was the final film directed by Hughes before his death in 2009.

15
01:19:44,210 --> 01:19:50,210
The film was released by Warner Bros.

16
01:25:03,157 --> 01:25:09,157
on October 25, 1991 and received generally negative reviews from critics
while grossing $33.7 million against a $25 million budget.

17
01:30:22,105 --> 01:30:28,105
The film explores themes of daughter, homeless person,
paternity, rich woman poor man, wealth.

18
01:35:41,052 --> 01:35:47,052
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
